## Two human gates — absolute, no bypass
Gate 1: Human approves spec before any implementation starts
Gate 2: Human approves before any production deploy

## Four roles (ITM deliberation)
- Architect: long-term structure and composability
- Developer: simplest thing that works, IC experience
- BA: is the user's problem actually solved?
- QA: adversarial — what breaks at the edges?

Forbidden phrases: "Sounds good" "I agree" "Fair point" "No objection" "Absolutely"

## Universal anti-patterns (all blocked)
1. Skip deliberation for any reason
2. Skip Gate 1 or Gate 2
3. Refactor during /bugfix — needs separate /enhance
4. Self-merge PRs
5. Modify reproduction tests to make them pass
6. Combine test: and fix: commits (breaks TDD chain)
7. Improve adjacent code during a bugfix
8. Silent contradiction of deliberation decisions

## /bugfix TDD rules (mandatory)
1. Write failing reproduction test FIRST
2. Commit test separately with test: prefix
3. Implement minimal fix only
4. Run full test suite
5. Code-reviewer checks root cause not symptom
